# Utilities, components, and `@apply`

Follow `design.md` → Components.

## Default: utilities first

Prefer Tailwind utilities for layout and UI composition. Use native elements and existing primitives before inventing structure.

## Ask before creating components

If you believe a **new** component is necessary, **ask the user first** and wait for permission. Do not create it proactively.

## Existing components stay naked

Once a component exists, do **not** put Tailwind utilities on it at the call site unless you ask and get permission.

Allowed without re-asking only when already documented (e.g. Button `variant`/`size`, Card `interactive`/`size`, Badge outline helpers / status tints).

Specializations: naked cards (`.cursor/rules/naked-cards.mdc`), naked headings (`.cursor/rules/naked-headings.mdc`).

## Repeated need → `@apply` in the component

If the same utilities would be needed repeatedly on a component, put them **inside the component** with `@apply` (co-located CSS or `@layer components`), then keep call sites naked. Do not copy-paste chrome utilities across call sites.

```tsx
// ✅
<div className="flex gap-2">
  <Button variant="outline">Deny</Button>
</div>

// ❌ without asking
<Button className="h-8 px-4">Deny</Button>
function NewWidget() { … }
```
